producer_report.summary:
Added `athena retry <job>`. It retries a rejected or failed job from that job's introspection record and shows the reading as `ask` does. Without a usable introspection record it falls back to plain "try again on" and says so on stderr. The CLI help test (retry shows `<JOB>`, `--yes`, `--json`) passes, and the full `cargo test --locked` run exited successfully. I could not read its output file, so I did not see per-test counts. `cargo fmt --all --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` also pass.

**How it works.**
- The stored request is "try again on <full id>", so later retry chains still find the original request.
- `earlier_attempt()` now also attaches a `RetryCause` when the job has a recorded rejection or failure introspection with a cause, prevention and proposed request. The latest such record is used.
- The reader brief gets a "Why it happened" section only when that record exists. It holds:
  - the cause, prevention and proposed next request;
  - the earlier cases of the same class, taken from the ids stored on the introspection, each with its job and a one-line account;
  - "Prevention already tried" for each earlier case that has one;
  - "This is case N of its class";
  - a note when an earlier prevention is identical to the current one.
- `Retry { job, yes, json }` in `main.rs` shares a new `show_proposal` helper with `Ask`, so the reading display, `--yes` and `--json` behave identically. Nothing runs unless the user accepts.
- A job that is not rejected or failed is refused before any model call, with "only a rejected or failed job can be tried again".
- A job with no usable introspection falls back to plain "try again on" and says so on stderr.

**Tests.**
- `crates/athena-cli/tests/retry.rs` has 5 fixture tests in temporary directories. They cover:
  - the seeded retry;
  - earlier cases and the already-tried prevention;
  - the no-earlier-case message;
  - the refusal of a job that is not rejected or failed;
  - the fallback.
- A unit test in `briefs.rs` shows the section appears only when the retry came from an introspection.
- The CLI help test is in the same file.

**Docs.** `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md` (command table and a paragraph) and a short "Built (step 2)" note in `docs/design/defaults-loop.md` section 12.

**Root cause.** The retry used to carry only the last findings, not the cause record. The fix reads the cause record in the one function both `ask "try again on"` and `retry` already share.
